# MCP integration (summary)

This patch adds a minimal Model Context Protocol (MCP) service and CLI helper.

What was added
- mcp/server/main.py : FastAPI MCP service (file-backed; optional Postgres via env)
- mcp/cli/announce_mcp.py : CLI to POST MCP records and optionally cosign + Rekor-upload
- scripts/hf_import_and_publish_mcp.py : wrapper around api.hf_importer.import_from_hf to import and then announce MCP

How to use (dev)
1. Run MCP server:
   AEGIS_MCP_STORE=/tmp/mcp_store.json uvicorn mcp.server.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8082

2. Import from HF and publish MCP:
   python scripts/hf_import_and_publish_mcp.py --repo-id google/flan-t5-small --model-name flan --version v1 --upload-s3 --register

3. To sign MCP JSON with cosign, ensure COSIGN_KEY env is set (KMS URI) and REKOR_SERVER if you want Rekor upload.

Notes
- In CI, set AEGIS_MCP_API and COSIGN_KEY as secrets and run the wrapper script during the promotion pipeline.
